    body: "LONDON/BUCHAREST – After seven strikes on cargo ships near NATO members Romania and Bulgaria last month, the U.S.-led military alliance said it would deploy maritime patrol aircraft, radars and drones to bolster its eastern flank in the Black Sea.\n\nThree days later, on Oct. 23, another ship was struck just outside Romanian waters. And last week a Greek container ship was sunk by naval drones in Bulgaria’s exclusive economic zone.\n\nUnabating attacks show how the escalating maritime war between Russia and Ukraine is expanding into a major challenge for NATO in the Black Sea that has left littoral member states such as Romania and Bulgaria exposed.",
